# Runs and data are artifacts, not source. Checkpoints go to HF Hub (M1+),
# metrics get published in write-ups, and neither belongs in git history.
#
# These MUST stay anchored with a leading slash. Written as `data/`, the pattern
# matches a directory of that name at any depth — which silently excluded the
# entire `src/microlab/data/` package from the repository. Everything still
# worked locally, and CI failed with `No module named 'microlab.data'`.
# tests/test_packaging.py::test_all_source_files_are_tracked guards this now.
/runs/
/data/
/outputs/
*.bin
*.manifest.json

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
